---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import '@/styles/prose.css';
import AmbientShapes from '@/components/layout/AmbientShapes.astro';

const developer = 'FizCode';
const contactEmail = 'fizcode@outlook.com';
const effectiveDate = '18 October 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="AniManga Info privacy policy | fizcode"
  description="What the AniManga Info Android app stores on your device, what it sends to MyAnimeList and AniList, and what it never collects."
>
  <AmbientShapes single />
  <section class="container policy">
    <header>
      <p class="type-eyebrow muted">AniManga Info · Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
      <h1 class="type-display-md">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="type-body-lg muted">
        AniManga Info is an Android app to browse anime and manga. This page explains what it does
        with your information. In short: it has no account, it shows no ads, and it does not send
        anything to the developer.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        The app is made by {developer}. If you have a question about this policy, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>No account, no data sent to the developer</h2>
      <p>
        You do not create an account or sign in. The app does not talk to any server of the
        developer, so the developer receives no information about you or how you use the app.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>The app keeps the following in its private storage on your phone:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your bookmarks.</strong> For each one: the title, poster link, type, rating and a few
          details of the anime or manga you saved.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your settings.</strong> The theme (system, light or dark), the titling style and the
          NSFW level you chose.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Whether you have seen the introduction</strong> shown when you first open the app.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of this is sent to the developer. You can remove it at any time by clearing the app's
        storage in the Android settings or by uninstalling the app. If you use Android's backup, your
        phone may include this data in your Google backup. That is controlled by Google and your device
        settings, not by the app.
      </p>

      <h2>What the app sends over the internet</h2>
      <p>
        The anime and manga information comes from two services. The app contacts them over a secure
        (HTTPS) connection:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://myanimelist.net" rel="noopener">MyAnimeList</a> for seasons, rankings, search
          and details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://anilist.co" rel="noopener">AniList</a> for extra details, cast, staff and
          characters.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>These requests contain:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the text you type in a search, and the anime or manga you open;</li>
        <li>
          the content setting you chose. When the NSFW level allows adult content, the request to
          MyAnimeList asks for it;
        </li>
        <li>an identifier of the app that MyAnimeList requires for its API.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Like every website or app you connect to, these services and the servers that deliver their
        images can see your IP address and basic technical details of the connection. The app does not
        send your name, email, location or any device identifier. How MyAnimeList and AniList handle
        what they receive is described in their own policies:
        <a href="https://myanimelist.net/about/privacy_policy" rel="noopener">MyAnimeList privacy policy</a>
        and <a href="https://anilist.co/terms" rel="noopener">AniList terms and privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What the app does not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No ads and no advertising ID.</li>
        <li>No analytics and no crash reporting.</li>
        <li>No location, contacts, photos, camera, microphone or files.</li>
        <li>No personal information of any kind is sold or shared by the developer.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        When you tap share on a synopsis, the app opens Android's share sheet with the text and a link
        to the anime or manga. You choose where it goes. The developer does not see it.
      </p>

      <h2>Adult content and age</h2>
      <p>
        The app can show media that MyAnimeList marks as suggestive (grey) or explicit (not safe). They
        are off by default, and the settings warn that they are meant for people of 17 and older, and
        21 and older. The app does not check or store your age. The app is not directed at children
        under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping and deleting your information</h2>
      <p>
        Your bookmarks and settings live only on your phone and stay until you clear the app's storage
        or uninstall it. The developer holds no copy, so there is nothing to ask the developer to
        delete.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the app starts to collect or share anything new, this page will be updated before the change
        reaches the app, and the effective date at the top will change.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-48);
    padding-block: var(--space-120) var(--space-140);
  }
  header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  header p, h1 { margin: 0; }

  /* The project pages turn the first line after a heading into a big lead; a policy reads as plain text */
  .policy :global(.prose h2) {
    font-size: var(--type-title-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-48);
  }
  .policy :global(.prose h2:first-child) { margin-top: 0; }
  .policy :global(.prose h2 + p) {
    font: var(--weight-regular) var(--type-body-md)/1.7 var(--font-body);
    letter-spacing: normal;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
  }
</style>
